text:
Audit of the standalone knowledge repository and tb-tools integration, 2026-10-06. Primary audience: tb-tools with Codex. Other agents should be able to consume the shared data and instructions without reducing primary functionality.

Snapshot before this audit contribution: 1218 notes, 6195 shared records, 1205 shared lessons (1105 Thunderbird and100 tb-tools). A fresh isolated store imported all shared files in5706ms. All lesson evidence dependencies were present; all supporting quotes matched. Five exact queries returned relevant code/style/workflow lessons in8–20ms.25 focused tests passed:22 knowledge/store/repository/CLI tests and3 mocked Codex injection/failure-isolation/native-memory tests. No live model quality benchmark or actual GitHub sync was tested.

Findings:
1. Shared memory data and console code are separated correctly. The local shared checkout has no origin and is not connected to a GitHub destination.
2. The publication path remains incomplete: service.capture keeps agent-turn evidence private; acceptLessons inherits the most restrictive evidence visibility; sync only exports shared records. Useful lessons from normal AI task evidence and imported history therefore do not automatically reach this repository. The manual backfill repaired existing content, not the normal producer.
3. A fresh shared-only index works and the lesson dependency graph is closed.454 lessons cite only historical summaries or shared notes; these preserve useful claims but do not independently confirm the original source.19 shared lesson records duplicate other lesson text. Query results can include a lesson, its Markdown-note record, and a recorded-lesson summary as separate hits, consuming context with repeated claims.
4.1731 shared records contain a personal absolute path:1721 CI observations refer to local cached evidence, and10 records are five historical summary/lesson pairs left from the interrupted backfill. A new clone cannot use another machine's evidence-cache paths.
5. Local status showed12946 pending extraction jobs and a reached daily budget. The default budget is four calls/day with at most six source slices/call. Shared-note records and historical summary records also enter the pending evidence queue.
6. Sync imports the complete Git tree and runs separate cat-file size/body processes for every file. At this snapshot that means more than14000 Git child processes per full-tree import, plus working-tree import. CLI inspection also reimports the shared checkout.
7. AGENTS.md, FORMAT.md and CONTRIBUTING.md support ordinary file/Git consumption and safe append-only contributions. There is no complete standalone schema/index-rebuild/consumer guide or component/style navigation catalog. The importer accepts only five named root documents plus notes and records; adding an ordinary new guide file would currently break strict tree sync.
8. Core knowledge modules, docs and focused tests exist as untracked tb-tools working files. They are usable in this local tree but are not part of committed distribution history.

Repair order proposed, not implemented by this evaluation: make useful project lesson publication a normal reliable API flow; retain private raw evidence while exporting scoped reusable knowledge and traceable sources; deduplicate retrieval and classify the learning queue; make import/sync incremental or use batch Git reads; document the record schema and consumer/index workflow; connect the chosen GitHub remote; preserve full Codex/SQLite/local semantic features and expose portable shared data; verify a second clean clone and a live Codex task. History study remains paused.

